{"id":"hotel-dieu-de-paris","name":"Hôtel-Dieu de Paris","qid":"Q1294736","country":"France","locality":"4th arrondissement of Paris","lat":"48.85463889","lon":"2.34880556","built":"1868","year":1868,"year_text":"1868","century":"19th century","era":"19th century","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"","heritage":"monument historique inscrit","type":"hospital; building complex; facility","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hôtel-Dieu_de_Paris","text":"The Hôtel-Dieu (French pronunciation: [otɛl djø]; \"God Shelter\") is a public hospital located on the Île de la Cité in the 4th arrondissement of Paris, on the parvis of Notre-Dame. Tradition has it that the hospital was founded by Saint Landry in 651 AD, but the first official records date it to 829, making it the oldest in France and possibly the oldest continuously operating hospital in the world. The Hôtel-Dieu was the only hospital in the city until the beginning of the 17th century.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H%C3%B4tel-Dieu_de_Paris","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-60d4fb14e368","w":1200,"h":560,"title":"Hôtel-Dieu from Tour Saint-Jacques.jpg","o":"gh-60d4fb14e368.jpg","credit":{"text":"Paris91 (remix); original by Jean-Christophe Windland","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:H%C3%B4tel-Dieu_from_Tour_Saint-Jacques.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-973395097647","w":1200,"h":1200,"title":"Hôtel-Dieu de Paris, February 7, 2013.jpg","o":"gh-973395097647.jpg","credit":{"text":"Groume","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:H%C3%B4tel-Dieu_de_Paris%2C_February_7%2C_2013.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-c34cfc26534f","w":1200,"h":800,"title":"Hôtel-Dieu de Paris from Notre-Dame de Paris, April 2011 001.jpg","o":"gh-c34cfc26534f.jpg","credit":{"text":"Cristian Bortes from Cluj-Napoca, Romania","license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:H%C3%B4tel-Dieu_de_Paris_from_Notre-Dame_de_Paris%2C_April_2011_001.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"assassins-creed-unity--hotel-dieu","game":"assassins-creed-unity","name":"Hotel-Dieu","verified":false,"text":"Hôtel-Dieu de Paris The Hôtel-Dieu de Paris is the oldest hospital in Paris, located on the Île de la Cité.","text_source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/H%C3%B4tel-Dieu","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-pe72e1a99140","w":1024,"h":1024,"o":"gh-pe72e1a99140.png","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Assassin's Creed Unity, © the game's publisher.","source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/File:ACUDB_-_Hotel-Dieu.png","via":"Fandom (assassinscreed)","note":"Fandom upload by Bovkaffe on 2017-12-27"}}]}]}